size_sweep_t8_gap_2026-08-10.tsv -- decode latency AND CPU across the size
ladder x thread count. Companion raw rows: size_sweep_t8_raw_2026-08-10.tsv.zst

WHAT WAS MISSING BEFORE THIS
  docs/SIZE_SWEEP.md measured the whole ladder at t=1 only ("t=1 for the whole
  ladder; only 1024x576 and 3840x2160 were also taken at t=8, and only at
  4:2:0"), and measured wall clock only -- no CPU. Per-image latency under
  threading, and the CPU price of it, were unmeasured.

HOST / BUILD
  Apple M4 Pro (Mac16,11, 8P+4E, 24 GB), macOS 26.5.2.
  rav1d-safe main @ 0f6bf10, release, default features, no target-cpu=native.
  dav1d 1.5.4 (homebrew), same interleaved sweep, rotating arm order.
  Measure-only: `git diff 0f6bf10..HEAD -- src/ lib.rs include/ crates/
  Cargo.toml Cargo.lock build.rs` is empty.

GRID
  6 sizes {64x36, 256x144, 512x288, 1024x576, 2048x1152, 3840x2160}
    x 2 depths {8, 10} bpc, YUV420, single tile          = 12 ladder vectors
  + 6 forced-multi-tile counterparts (2x2 and 4x2)       = 18 vectors
  x threads {1, 2, 4, 8}
  x arms {rs, dav1d_fd1 (--framedelay 1), dav1d_def (default frame delay)}
  x 9 rounds.  Frame counts per cell: 2500/25000 at 64x36 .. 2/16 at 4K.

INSTRUMENT
  bash `time` keyword, TIMEFORMAT='%3R %3U %3S' -- the child's getrusage as the
  kernel reports it. Two frame counts per cell; `total = a + b*frames` fitted
  SEPARATELY for wall and for user+sys, so process startup (exec, mmap,
  container parse, decoder construction, thread-pool spin-up) drops out of both.
  cores busy = (cpu ms/frame) / (wall ms/frame).
  Speedups, CPU multipliers and ours/dav1d ratios are paired within a round,
  then median with the min/max band.

CORRECTNESS BEFORE TIMING
  size_sweep_t8_vector_md5_2026-08-10.tsv       30/30 bit-identical to dav1d
  size_sweep_t8_thread_invariance_2026-08-10.tsv 18/18 identical across t=1..8
  size_sweep_tile_layout_2026-08-10.tsv          tile counts, read from the
                                                 frame header, not the recipe

LOAD TAG -- READ THIS BEFORE QUOTING ANY ABSOLUTE
  Every row carries foreign_max. The box was NOT idle: a second agent's miri run
  plus its own timed gap sweep were live throughout. This happened partly
  because measlock's EXIT trap deletes the lock directory unconditionally, even
  when the lock has since been reclaimed by another holder -- see
  docs/SIZE_SWEEP_T8.md. Absolutes are inflated; paired within-round ratios are
  the usable statistics.

COMMANDS
  scripts/perf/tile_layout.py         ~/tmp/t8gap/ivf
  scripts/perf/size_sweep_t8.sh       (BIN/AVIF/IVF/ARMS/CELLS via env)
  scripts/perf/size_sweep_t8_report.py <raw.tsv> --tsv <this.tsv>
  scripts/perf/size_sweep_t8_amdahl.py <this.tsv>
